// Counting work, for the constraints (docs/TESTS.md, "Constraints are counted,
// not timed"): `time` is one per function call and loop iteration plus the
// bytes the runtime's helpers touch, `mem` the bytes each allocation requests.
//
// idc.py splices counters into the text of its runtime. Here the runtime is a
// generated literal (../../../../../runtime/prelude.id), so the counting is
// wrapped around it with the preprocessor instead:
//
//   * every allocation the runtime makes goes through id_alloc, id_realloc or
//     the list-growth path, each of which names the bytes it was asked for to
//     ID_MEM_CHARGE, so `mem` is what was requested (the pool's chunks are
//     malloc'd whole and are not the program's work);
//   * a string carries its length, so no runtime helper measures one any more
//     and nothing is left to hook: `concat` charges both operands and `len`
//     the string, as they always were, by being renamed out of the way before
//     the runtime and redefined after it with the charge added. `character_code_at` is
//     one load and is not charged;
//   * strlen is still hooked, for the one helper that reads a C buffer (input).
//
// The hooks are undone after the runtime: nothing else calls them, and the
// harness's own bookkeeping is not the program's work.

emit_count(string ind) {
  if((import harn)[0] == 1) {
    print(ind + "id_ctr_time++;");
  }
} return void;
given entry_fixture_harn (" "):() then prints:(" id_ctr_time++;\n")
given entry_fixture_harn ("    "):() then prints:("    id_ctr_time++;\n")
given harn_init (" "):() then prints:("")

